*** Add File:ops/runbooks/TRITON_DEPLOY_RUNBOOK.md
+# Triton LLM Deployment Runbook (step-by-step)
+
+Prereqs
+- Kubernetes cluster with GPU nodes and NVIDIA device plugin installed.
+- PVC (ReadWriteMany) for triton model repository (we provide k8s/triton/pvc.yaml).
+- Container registry for images (update image names in k8s manifests).
+- kubeconfig with permissions.
+
+Steps
+1. Export model to ONNX
+   - Run locally or via CI:
+     python ops/onnx/export_hf_to_onnx.py --model gpt2 --out-dir out/model_repo/gpt2/1
+   - Verify model.onnx exists and tokenizer files saved in same dir.
+
+2. Stage model into Triton PVC
+   - Copy the folder out/model_repo/gpt2/1 into the mounted PVC path (e.g., using a Kubernetes Job or mount on a bastion).
+   - Final layout on PVC: /models/gpt2/1/model.onnx and tokenizer files and config.pbtxt in /models/gpt2
+
+3. Apply Triton manifests
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/triton/pvc.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/triton/deployment.yaml
+   kubectl apply -f k8s/inference/inference-gateway-update.yaml
+
+4. Validate
+   - Run ops/triton/validate_triton_inference.py (adjust tokens to match tokenizer).
+   - Check Triton server logs and model load status:
+     kubectl -n inference logs deploy/triton-inference -c triton-server
+
+5. Safety & telemetry
+   - Ensure inference gateway is fronting Triton and policy/hard-constraints are enabled.
+   - Configure Prometheus scrape (monitoring/prometheus/speculative-scrape-config.yaml) to capture orchestration metrics and Triton metrics.
+   - Run a small locust test (ops/tests/locust_speculative_locustfile.py adapted to /infer route) and monitor latency and GPU telemetry.
+
+6. Canary & promotion
+   - Use services/ci/canary_runner.py to deploy candidate and compare outputs against baseline.
+   - Integrate canary checks with safe_promotion_controller for gated promotion.
+
+Notes & Troubleshooting
+- If model fails to load, inspect config.pbtxt and ONNX input/output names (use onnxruntime/tools to inspect graph).
+- For token-by-token generation you may need to export a model shape that returns logits for next-token given input_ids.
+- Triton model config must match the ONNX graph's input names and shapes exactly.
+
